==Battleground==
*10 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Doctor K.O.]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Winged Pigge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**8 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Hackey]] spawns.
**3 [[Doctor K.O.]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
**5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**2 [[Great Angel Chibinel]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A rather straightforward stage. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is basically a necessity given all of the Angels here. Kill the first wave of peons and send [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Catcrates]] to paralyze Winged Pigge while using [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], and other anti-Angel heavy hitters to turn the Pigge into some angelic bacon. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can take care of the Red enemies while you're busy doing that. Once you can get a good Freeze chain going on Winged Pigge, time [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] + the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to chunk her and get rid of her even faster. Her death effectively means victory, since Boraphim alone can't do much to get past all of your anti-Angels.

==Trivia==
*The バラン ''Baran'' in Plastic Pastures' Japanese name (バラバラバラン草原 ''Barabara Baran Sōgen'', "Scattered Baran Grassland") refers to ''[[wikipedia:ja:人造バラン|jinzō baran]]'' (人造バラン), the [https://sushiuniversity.jp/basicknowledge/what-is-the-green-jagged-sheet-placed-in-between-sushi-and-sashimi green, jagged sheet] placed in between sushi and sashimi.

